Smart Taxi Backend API

A Node.js backend for a ride-hailing platform. The API supports passengers, drivers, and administrators, with ride management, driver dispatch, authentication, notifications, and real-time ride offers.

Features

Authentication and account security

Public registration creates passenger accounts by default; drivers use the driver-specific workflows after an account has been provisioned.

Login for registered users.

Short-lived JWT access tokens and refresh-token rotation.

Password hashing with bcrypt.

Role-based authorization for PASSENGER, DRIVER, and ADMIN users.

Profile updates and password changes.

Refresh-token revocation on logout and security-sensitive account actions.

Administrative user blocking and unblocking.

Ride and driver workflows

Passenger ride requests with pickup and destination coordinates.

Ride lifecycle management: PENDING, ACCEPTED, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED, and CANCELLED.

Driver availability management (OFFLINE, ONLINE, and BUSY) and location updates.

Driver vehicle registration and management.

Ride filtering by ride type and driver eligibility.

Location-based driver selection using Haversine distance calculations.

Expanding dispatch search stages: 3 km, 5 km, and 10 km.

Vehicle compatibility rules: NORMAL vehicles receive NORMAL rides; COMFORT vehicles can receive both ride types.

Concurrency and data consistency

Ride acceptance is handled in a Sequelize database transaction. The service locks the ride row, checks that the ride is still pending, validates the driver's eligibility, assigns the ride, and changes the driver's status to BUSY within the same transaction. Conditional updates provide an additional safeguard against competing acceptance requests.

Real-time communication and notifications

Socket.IO connections are authenticated with a JWT supplied during the handshake.

Passenger and driver private rooms are derived from the authenticated server-side user identity.

Real-time ride offers are sent to eligible connected drivers.

The passenger can receive a ride:no-driver-found event when the final dispatch stage ends without an eligible driver.

Persisted notifications can also be delivered through the notification:new event.

API documentation and validation

Interactive Swagger UI at /api-docs.

Request validation with express-validator.

Centralized error handling.

Security headers with Helmet and configurable CORS.

Rate limiting on authentication endpoints.

